<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/"><channel><title>Stockholm D&amp;D</title><link>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/</link><description>Recent content on Stockholm D&amp;D</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://stockholmdnd.github.io/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Character Creation</title><link>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/character-creation/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/character-creation/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;To help you create a character that is Stockholm D&amp;amp;D Legal, we have included a step-by-step process both for those who use D&amp;amp;DBeyond and those who do not. If you are familiar with D&amp;amp;D 5.5e, you can simply read the summary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are new to D&amp;amp;D, we strongly recommend that you choose a character without spellcasting, i.e. Barbarian or Fighter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="a-summary-of-our-character-creation-rules"&gt;A summary of our character creation rules&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start at level 3.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Any official D&amp;amp;D-source from the &lt;a href="https://stockholmdnd.github.io/dnd/5-5e/source"&gt;approved list&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Point buy or Standard array. (Rolling for stats is not permitted.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixed hit-points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Starting equipment, one common magic item from the &lt;a href="https://stockholmdnd.github.io/dnd/5-5e/magic-items"&gt;magic items list&lt;/a&gt;, + 100gp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feats and Multi-classing are allowed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You may come from any D&amp;amp;D-esque world, including homebrew; we are setting agnostic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow the spirit of the game, have fun together, don’t cheat or try to find loopholes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are responsible for your character, be mindful of the whole table.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item><item><title>Registering your character</title><link>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/registration/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/registration/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;We use a Discord bot to manage participation at our events, so you must register your character with &lt;code&gt;@D&amp;amp;Dtabler&lt;/code&gt; from our Discord server before you can join a table.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Playing your first game</title><link>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/playing/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/playing/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Before your first adventure, make sure your character is Guild-legal and that you&amp;rsquo;ve signed up for an event and joined a table.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sensitive subjects and discomfort</title><link>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/sensitive-subjects/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/sensitive-subjects/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Games may involve subjects or depictions that make a player uncomfortable; if anything could be triggering, let the Dungeon Master know before the session starts.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Rewards</title><link>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/rewards/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/rewards/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Every adventure you play in Stockholm D&amp;amp;D is worth half a level, as long as your character survives the adventure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;aside class="phb-note"&gt;
You start at level 3. After surviving 2 adventures (0.5 levels each) you will be level 4.
&lt;/aside&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After each adventure, the Dungeon Master decides how much gold the party gets, based on the tier played:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Tier&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Level played&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Standard gold&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th scope="col"&gt;Maximum gold&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3-4&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;100&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;150&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5-6&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;150&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;225&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;7-8&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;230&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;345&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;9-10&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;340&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;510&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;11-12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;510&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;765&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;6&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;13-14&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;760&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1140&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;7&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;15-16&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1140&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1710&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;17-18&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1710&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2565&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;9&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;19-20&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2560&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3840&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2 id="acquiring-loot-on-adventures"&gt;Acquiring loot on adventures&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may acquire permanent and consumable magic items in your adventures. Permanent magic items acquired in a session can never be carried out of that session. Consumable magic items can, but this must be explicitly stated by the Dungeon Master, who should specify what the item is and how many times it can be used before it is consumed.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Shopping</title><link>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/shopping/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/shopping/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Before going on an adventure, you may buy any item listed in the PHB at its listed price, along with the healing potions, potions, and spell scrolls described here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="healing-potions"&gt;Healing potions&lt;/h3&gt;
