&lt;h3 id="selling-items"&gt;Selling items&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Items sold back to the Guild fetch half their listed price.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Before each adventure</title><link>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/preparation/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/preparation/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The expectation is that you arrive at the table with your character sheet sorted: items chosen, downtime resolved, features understood, and any spells picked.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Downtime</title><link>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/downtime/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/downtime/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;After your character has survived an adventure, you may perform one downtime activity — crafting an item, scribing a spell, learning a language or tool, silvering a weapon, buying a poison, or buying life insurance.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>If you are unhappy with your character</title><link>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/rerolls/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/rerolls/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Before your character reaches level 5, you may change a few things — subspecies, subclass, class features, background, feats, ability score increases, chosen spells, and descriptive details.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>General clarifications</title><link>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/faq/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://stockholmdnd.github.io/player-guide/faq/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Some rules and rules interactions can be confusing; we ask that you first look to the &lt;a href="https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/sae"&gt;Sage Advice compendium&lt;/a&gt; for official rulings before raising a question with us.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item